# Code owners — review routing.
#
# The default owner reviews everything. The paths below carry safety-critical
# LEGAL data (criminal sanctions, deontic force, court holdings, EU-directive
# transposition) where a heuristic error has real-world consequences. Changes to
# them require legal-correctness sign-off per CONTRIBUTING.md ("Mandatory
# legal-correctness review"). When a dedicated legal-domain reviewer joins, add
# their handle alongside @henrikaavik on these lines so GitHub requests their
# review automatically.
#
# The generator lines point at the implementation modules under `src/estleg/`,
# not at the same-named entry points in `scripts/` — those are thin `runpy`
# shims with no extraction logic, so routing them here would have requested a
# legal review for nothing while the real heuristics changed under the default
# owner (#685). `tests/test_codeowners.py` keeps every path below pointing at a
# real, non-shim file.

# Default owner for everything in the repo.
